{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And he cursed his day</b> — Although a day cannot receive blessing or curse, therefore out of great distress the sufferer says: Cursed be the day on which he was born and the hour in which he was born. Also there are days that are such when both luminaries are in a harsh alignment, and this requires a long explanation. So too Jeremiah said: Cursed be the day wherein I was born. Some say that it refers to the day of the week, that he longed that its memory not be heard — it is the day on which he was born. But the correct interpretation is the first."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:32.753713183Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}